{"name":"Blue Echo","hex":"#8dbbc9","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"echo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Echo of the ICAO/NATO radiotelephony alphabet."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A reflected sound that is heard again by its initial observer.","An utterance repeating what has just been said."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/echo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Finger-Style Guitar","blocks":[{"text":"Finger-Style Guitar is the sixth studio album by American guitarist Chet Atkins, released in 1956."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/ec/Finger_Style_Guitar_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finger-Style_Guitar"},{"title":"Echo","blocks":[{"text":"In audio signal processing and acoustics, an echo is a reflection of sound that arrives at the listener with a delay after the direct sound. The delay is directly proportional to the distance of the reflecting surface from the source and the listener. Typical examples are the echo produced by the bottom of a well, a building, or the walls of enclosed and empty rooms."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Echo"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans 